A||||7||Lynx||4cyl to V6 conversion||||5
Z||000000||Lynx||09-30-1999||11:37 PM||||Ok I just bought a 85 GT today for only a $100 of course the engine knocks and the automatic trans dont have 2nd gear. The body is good though and it was way worth $100. What i want to do is use it for a parts car and pull the V6 (rebuild it)and put it in my 85 SC. Ok my car has the isuzu 5 speed will that bolt to the V6. Also what do i do for a computer swap, since the V6 was bolted to a auto and im putting it into a manual.||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||10-01-1999||08:25 PM||||you need to change the prom in the ECM. has to be out of another ECM of the same type. some one said the ECM changed in either 85 or 86 so you have to watch out you don't get the wrong one.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||10-03-1999||12:20 PM||||The 85 computer is a 6869. The 86 and up is the 7170. The manual vs auto chips are different. The chips can not be swapped between ECM's (you can't put a 6869 chip in a 7170). Be sure to get the little chip too (the backup fuel chips) in case they are different. You can't swap between ECM's.<P>Actually, the two ECM's are essentially the same, but some hardware was removed or added between the two. The 6869 has the turbo code, but is missing the wastegate driver chip. The 7170 lost both. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-04-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||10-03-1999||12:22 PM||||You should compare the 6869 and 7170 wiring. I don't have my 85 manual here, but it seems to me the was one small wiring change. If you can get the wiring harness for the engine, it should just about swap in. The V6's had the additional cooling fan too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||TOM||10-03-1999||06:51 PM||||What do you mean it has the turbo code still in it. Does it add more fuel if there is zero vacumm as in a boost condition?||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||10-04-1999||01:57 AM||||Duplicate message.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-04-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||10-04-1999||01:58 AM||||The turbo code has to be basically enabled (two bar map, some other stuff). The stock Fiero code for the 6869 just operates in good ol' one bar mode. Fueling is done the same way with a one or two bar map (boost). ||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||10-04-1999||02:18 AM||||Hi Tom,<P>I'm not sure what you mean by "extra fuel with zero vacuum" (paraphrased). At either WOT (~100kPA) or under boost (&gt;100kPA), the fueling is still handled as a target AFR (12:1). Since the O2 is not in control of the fuel in power enrichment, that target might or might not be hit. The injector pulse width is increased to what the ECM thinks will give 12:1 based on the RPM and  injector size and VE of the engine. Probably pretty close though.<P>Fuel is added when you go into acceleration enrichment (change in throttle position) or power enrichment (throttle above a certain position) regardless of the map reading. It is added based on RPM and coolant temp. ||||reg||1
